:: Mansion Intro
<<avery_mansion_init>>
<<set $location to "avery_mansion">><<set $outside to 0>><<effects>>

<<npc "Avery">><<person1>>
<<earnFeat "Kept">>

Avery turns off Danube Street, and drives down a well-tended boulevard. The tall spruces are of a different species to those found in the nearby forest. They flit past the window, obscuring the unique homes behind them as the road twists up a hill.
<br><br>

Avery's mansion waits at the top. <<He>> doesn't slow as the filigree gates open, and drives into a tasteful garden, surrounded by tall walls. <<He>> continues into a garage, and parks beside a second car.
<br><br>

<<He>> kills the engine, and steps outside.
<br><br>

<<link [[Wait|Mansion Intro Wait]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Climb out|Mansion Intro Climb]]>><<npcincr Avery dom 1>><</link>><<gdom>>
<br>

:: Mansion Intro Wait
<<effects>>

You remain seated. Avery steps around the front bonnet, opens your door, and offers <<his>> arm.
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Mansion Intro 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Mansion Intro Climb
<<effects>>

You try to open the door, but it's locked. Avery flashes a smile as <<he>> steps around the front bonnet, opens your door, and offers <<his>> arm.
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Mansion Intro 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Mansion Intro 2
<<effects>>

You step out of the car. "I hope you liked the drive here," <<he>> says. "It's a pleasant neighbourhood. You won't have to worry about being harassed outside. Come, let me show you around."
<br><br>
<<He>> shuts the garage door as <<he>> walks towards the entrance, an uncharacteristic spring in <<his>> step.
<<npcincr Avery rage -10>><<lllarage>><<set C.npc.Avery.rage to Math.clamp(C.npc.Avery.rage, 0, 50)>>
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Mansion Intro 3]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Mansion Intro 3
<<effects>>

The door opens onto a spacious kitchen. Avery gestures as <<he>> gives you a breakdown of where to find each appliance. The surfaces are spotless, the machines state-of-the-art.
<br><br>

"The dining room is through here," <<he>> says, leading you beneath a wide arch. A row of tall windows dominate the far wall, letting ample natural light fall over a long dining table. You count eighteen seats.
<br><br>

<<link [[Ask if Avery has guests often|Mansion Intro 3 Ask]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Remain quiet|Mansion Intro 3 Quiet]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Mansion Intro 3 Ask
<<effects>>

<<speechresolve>>
<<if $speech_attitude_avery>>
	<<set _speechAttitudeResolved to "meek">>
<</if>>
<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy")>>
	"There's a lot of chairs here," you say. "Will I be meeting lots of guests?"
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
	"Do you entertain often?" you ask, eyeing the long table. "It looks made for company."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
	"Should I remember where to sit?" you ask, looking over the chairs. "For when people visit."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
	"You must host a lot," you say, letting your gaze travel along the table.
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
	"You must be popular," you say, waving a hand at the chairs. "To need seating for so many guests."
<<else>>
	"Do you have a lot of guests?" you ask.
<</if>>
<br><br>

Avery nods. "I like to throw parties," <<he>> says. "I get temporary help for cooking and such, on those occasions. Come, let me show you the lounge."
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Mansion Intro 4]]>><</link>>
<br>


:: Mansion Intro 3 Quiet
<<effects>>

You remain quiet. Avery pauses by the head of the table, noticing the direction of your stare even without a question. <<He>> points at the far end. "That's your seat," <<he>> says. "Except when we have guests. Then it's here." <<He>> rests a hand on the chair beside <<him>>, already arranging you in <<his>> head.
<br><br>

"Come, let me show you the lounge."
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Mansion Intro 4]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Mansion Intro 4
<<effects>>

The lounge is even more well-lit than the dining room, more spacious than the kitchen. Modern furniture and decorations are arranged in a tasteful, fashionable way, centred on a large screen hanging from one wall.
<br><br>

A sleek black piano sits tucked away in the corner of the room.
<<if $hallucinations gte 1>>
	Its ivory keys contrast against its body like bright teeth, flashing you an inviting smile. <<stress 2>><<gstress>>
<<else>>
	It's freshly dusted, but looks like it hasn't seen use in a long time.
<</if>>
<br><br>

"This is where I relax," Avery says, reclining on a sofa. "A rare event." <<He>> stands, and strides over to a cabinet across the room. "Can I offer you a drink?"
<br><br>

<<if playerIsPregnant() and playerAwareTheyArePregnant()>>
	<span class="blue">You can't bring yourself to drink while you know you're with child.</span>
<<else>>
	<<link [[Nod|Mansion Intro 4 Drink]]>><<drunk 60>><</link>><<gdrunk>>
<</if>>
<br>
<<link [[Refuse|Mansion Intro 4 Refuse]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Mansion Intro 4 Drink
<<effects>><<wearProp "fizzy drink">>

Avery opens the cabinet, then a colourful bottle, and pours into two thimble-sized glasses. <<He>> hands one to you.
<br><br>

The drink is as colourful as the bottle, and smells strong. "Just a little," <<he>> says, before downing <<his>> glass. <<He>> examines the empty vessel. "I'd like you to remember the tour."
<br><br>

You swallow the drink. It's stronger than it smells, burning bright on your tongue before the sweetness catches up. You shudder. Avery watches with amusement.
<br><br>

<<link [[Let <<him>> continue|Mansion Intro 5]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Ask about the piano|Mansion Intro Piano]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Mansion Intro 4 Refuse
<<effects>>

<<speechresolve>>
<<if $speech_attitude_avery>>
	<<set _speechAttitudeResolved to "meek">>
<</if>>
<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy")>>
	"No, thank you," you say, keeping your hands close to yourself.
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
	"I'll pass for now, thank you," you say.
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
	"Not right now," you say. "If that's all right."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
	"Not for me," you say, leaving no room for fuss.
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty">>
	"I'll skip the tiny drink," you say.
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel">>
	"No thanks," you say. "I'd like to keep my judgement."
<<else>>
	"No, thank you," you say.
<</if>>
<br><br>

Avery opens the cabinet, takes out a colourful bottle, and pours into a thimble-sized glass for <<himself>>. <<He>> looks out the window as <<he>> sips it.
<br><br>

<<link [[Let <<him>> continue|Mansion Intro 5]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Ask about the piano|Mansion Intro Piano]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Mansion Intro Piano
<<effects>>
<<speechresolve>>
<<if $speech_attitude_avery>>
	<<set _speechAttitudeResolved to "meek">>
<</if>>
<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy")>>
	"That piano is gorgeous," you say with a hint of awe. "How often do you play it?"
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
	"The piano is beautiful," you say. "Do you play much?"
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
	"It's lovely," you say. "The piano, I mean. Do you play?"
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
	"That piano looks too expensive to be decorative," you say. "Do you play?"
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
	"Nice piano," you say. "Is it only here to make the room look cultured? Do you play it?"
<<else>>
	"That's a really nice piano," you say. "How often do you play it?"
<</if>>
<br><br>

Avery frowns, but it's brief. "I don't." <<He>> pauses. "Anymore. I've been meaning to get rid of it."
<br><br>

<<He>> stares at the piano as if it were about to come alive, but manages to tear <<his>> eyes away. <<He>> gestures at a door opposite the dining room.
"Through there is the display room." The interior is dark, but you spy a statuette on a plinth. "I keep valuable antiques there. Don't enter without a reason." <<He>> waves <<his>> hand, as if dismissing the room as unimportant.
<br><br>

"Let me show you our bedroom." <<He>> leads you into an atrium, lit by a skylight far above. An ornate staircase leads to the second storey, which forks left and right. Avery turns left.
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Mansion Intro 6]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Mansion Intro 5
<<effects>>

"Through there is the display room," Avery says, gesturing at a door opposite the dining room. The interior is dark, but you spy a statuette on a plinth. "I keep valuable antiques there. Don't enter without a reason." <<He>> waves <<his>> hand, as if dismissing the room as unimportant.
<br><br>

"Let me show you our bedroom." <<He>> leads you into an atrium, lit by a skylight far above. An ornate staircase leads to the second storey, which forks left and right. Avery turns left.
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Mansion Intro 6]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Mansion Intro 6
<<effects>>

"Guest rooms," Avery says as you pass by a succession of closed doors. "Mostly. Some are storage." <<He>> stops in front of an ornate wood door, and reaches into <<his>> pocket.
<br><br>
"Here." <<He>> holds out a key. "I had a second made. Go on, open it."
<br><br>

You open the door, revealing a large bedroom. A four-poster bed stands in the corner. Beside it is a glass door, leading onto a balcony. There's a hot tub on the other side. Opposite the bed are two more doors.
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Mansion Intro 7]]>><</link>>
<br>


:: Mansion Intro 7
<<effects>>

"This is my room," Avery says. "Our room." <<He>> strides through, and opens one of the doors. Inside is a bathroom, with a large bath. Avery moves to the next, revealing a walk-in cupboard.
<<if $pronoun is "m">>
	Dozens of expensive suits hang inside, alongside rows of shoes.
<<else>>
	Dozens of expensive suits and dresses hang inside, alongside rows of shoes.
<</if>>
<br><br>

"Plenty of space," <<he>> says. "Should you want a large wardrobe. Come. Let me show you my study."
<br><br>

<span class="gold">Some fancy clothes have been added to your wardrobe.</span>
<br><br>

<<if perceivedGenderBinary() is C.npc.Avery.pronoun or (genderIsIgnored() and !playerIsXChanged() and $player.sex is C.npc.Avery.pronoun and random(0,100) lt 25)>>
	<<link [[Next|Mansion Intro XChange]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	<<link [[Next|Mansion Intro 8]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Mansion Intro XChange
<<effects>>

	Right before leaving, you spot an ornate-looking ivory chest, small enough to contain maybe all kinds of jewelry, but still large enough to be conspicuous at the top of the dresser it is placed on. Noticing your gaze, Avery moves over to pick it up. "Right. I almost forgot," <<he>> opens the box. "Here's your new pill."
	<br><br>
	/* The spare pill has to suit the body you'll be left with once any current pill ends, so read the sex off the stored body while pilled and off the live body otherwise. */
	<<set _pcTrueSex to (playerIsXChanged() ? ($xchange.pill.originalBody?.sex ?? $player.sex) : $player.sex)>>
	<<set _variant to (_pcTrueSex is "m") ? "(F)" : "(M)">>
	/* Avery objects to being seen with a partner who reads as the same sex, so compare what the public reads off each of you */
	<<set _sameSexAsAvery to perceivedGenderBinary() is C.npc.Avery.pronoun>>
	<<if !playerIsXChanged() and _sameSexAsAvery and $player.sex isnot C.npc.Avery.pronoun>>
		<<He>> stops with the pill between <<his>> fingers and looks you over again. "No. Your body is fine. It's how you've presented yourself."
		<br><br>
		<<He>> closes the chest with a decisive snap and puts the pill away. "Change into something more <<if C.npc.Avery.pronoun is "m">>feminine<<else>>masculine<</if>><<if C.npc.Avery.pronoun is "f" and ($makeup.lipstick or $makeup.eyeshadow or $makeup.mascara)>>, and take off that makeup while you're at it<</if>>. I won't be seen out with someone who looks like me." <<stress 5>><<gstress>>
	<<elseif xchangePregnancyBlocksPill()>>
		Just as <<hes>> about to give you the pill, <<he>> raises an eyebrow as <<his>> eyes travel down over you, then back up. The pill pauses between <<his>> fingers. <<He>> clicks <<his>> tongue. "Pregnant. I hate babies. They make everything messy with consequences, questions, noise. What a complication."
		<br><br>
		<<He>> holds the pill out anyway and closes the chest with a decisive snap. "No pill while you're carrying. You take care of the baby first, then you swallow this. <span class="red">You must swallow this</span>. Understand?" | <span class="blue">+1 Choice pill</span><<stress 5>><<gstress>>
		<<set $sexStats.pills["pills"]["X-Change Choice "+_variant].owned++>><<set $sexStats.pills.boughtOnce to true>>
	<<elseif xchangePillProtectionActive()>>
		It's not up for discussion. A foregone conclusion. <span class="pink"><<He>> simply feeds the pill to you</span>, paying no attention to any protest or objection you might have. Perhaps instinctively, you know better. | <span class="red">You get spiked by a choice pill.</span><<trauma 5>><<gtrauma>>
		<<silently>><<xchange-effects 1 `[]`>><</silently>>
	<<elseif !playerIsXChanged()>>
		It's not up for discussion. A foregone conclusion. <span class="pink"><<He>> simply feeds the pill to you</span>, paying no attention to any protest or objection you might have. Perhaps instinctively, you know better. | <span class="red">You get spiked by a choice pill.</span><<trauma 5>><<gtrauma>>
		<<xchange-choice>><<set $averytimespilled += 1>>
	<<elseif !_sameSexAsAvery>>
		Since you're pilled already, this pill would have no effect. "For when your current pill expires, I mean," Avery clarifies. "<span class="pink">...If it ever does</span>." <<He>> presses it into your hand. | <span class="blue">+1 Choice pill</span>
		<<set $sexStats.pills["pills"]["X-Change Choice "+_variant].owned++>><<set $sexStats.pills.boughtOnce to true>>
	<<elseif _pcTrueSex is C.npc.Avery.pronoun>>
		/* Pilled, still reads as the same sex, and the body underneath matches too, so the spare pill is still the right one to take afterwards. */
		<<He>> stops with the pill between <<his>> fingers and looks you over again. "You're already pilled. Into this."
		<br><br>
		<<He>> presses it into your hand rather than feeding it to you. "Whatever you took, get off it. Then swallow this one. <span class="red">I won't be seen out with someone who looks like me</span>. Understand?" | <span class="blue">+1 Choice pill</span><<stress 5>><<gstress>>
		<<set $sexStats.pills["pills"]["X-Change Choice "+_variant].owned++>><<set $sexStats.pills.boughtOnce to true>>
	<<else>>
		/* The pill they're on is what made them match Avery. Reverting is the fix, so handing over a pill that flips their real body would only make it worse. */
		<<He>> stops with the pill between <<his>> fingers and looks you over again. "You're already pilled. Into this."
		<br><br>
		<<He>> closes the chest with a decisive snap and puts the pill away. "You were fine as you were. <span class="red">Get off whatever that is, as soon as you can, and stay off it.</span> I won't be seen out with someone who looks like me." <<stress 5>><<gstress>>
	<</if>>
	<br><br>

	<<speechresolve>>
	<<if $speech_attitude_avery>>
		<<set _speechAttitudeResolved to "meek">>
	<</if>>
	<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy")>>
		"I-Is it... safe?" you ask. "What is it?"
	<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
		"What kind of pill is it?" you ask. "Is it safe?"
	<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
		"I'll take it if you say so," you say. "But... what is it?"
	<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
		"You should tell me what it does before you hand it over," you say. "What is it?"
	<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty">>
		"You forgot to mention the mysterious pill part of the tour," you say. "What is it?"
	<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel">>
		"How reassuring," you say, looking at the pill. "A surprise from a locked box. What is it?"
	<<else>>
		"What is it?" you ask.
	<</if>>
	<br><br>

	Avery answers as if <<he>> had been waiting for the question. "I managed to get my hands on one of these government-issued <span class="gold">Choice pills</span>. Same kind they use for <i>rehabilitation</i> facilities." <<His>> voice betrays a hint of pride. "So don't worry. It is perfectly safe."
	<br><br>

	/* Avery dismisses identity either way, but a nonbinary PC needs their own wording: "you're trans" doesn't fit someone who never crossed between the two. */
	<<set _pcEnby to (playerFeltGender() is "n" and !$background.transgender)>>
	<<if $background.transgender or playerFeltGender() is "n">>
		<<if !$transgenderknown.includes("Avery")>>
			<<run $transgenderknown.pushUnique("Avery")>>
			<<if _pcEnby>>You tell Avery that you're neither a man nor a woman, and that swapping your body between the two will not make you either.<<else>>You tell Avery that you're trans, and that changing your body will not change who you are.<</if>> "I understand what you're saying," <<he>> says coldly.
		<<else>>
			<<if _pcEnby>>You remind Avery that swapping your body between the two will not make you one.<<else>>You remind Avery that changing your body does not change who you are.<</if>> "I heard you the first time," <<he>> says coldly.
		<</if>>
		"You can call yourself whatever you like. If you're living under my roof, you'll look the way I expect."
		<br><br>
	<</if>>

	"Come. Let's continue," <<he>> concludes.
	<br><br>


<<link [[Next|Mansion Intro 8]]>><</link>>
<br>


:: Mansion Intro 8
<<effects>>

Avery's study is on the third storey, and locked as well, but <<he>> doesn't offer you a key. The interior is small. A single desk, chair, and computer sit surrounded by bookshelves on all sides. You follow Avery inside. You feel as if the tall, laden shelves are about to fall and crush you.
<br><br>

You're struck by an odd discrepancy between rooms. Most are modern, spacious and well-lit. Others, like this study, feel older, and enclosed. Small spaces tucked away, easily missed.
<br><br>

"I keep it locked for security," Avery says. "Some of the books have value. Just ask me if you want to read anything. I'll let you in."
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Mansion Intro 9]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Mansion Intro 9
<<effects>>

Avery leads you back downstairs, through the lounge, and a door leading outside.
<br><br>

"The pool," Avery says, letting it speak for itself. It's almost as big as the one at school.
<br><br>

<<He>> looks out at the pool, garden, and the far wall beyond. "It's almost a shame I work so much. I'm not here to enjoy it enough. <span class="gold">Could you be sure to greet me when I get home?</span> I finish at <<ampm 21 00>> weekdays and <<ampm 17 00>> Sunday."
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Mansion Intro 9 Dinner]]>><</link>>

:: Mansion Intro 9 Dinner
<<effects>>

"<span class="gold">Have dinner ready for me too.</span> I think I'd like a <span class="gold">hamburger</span>, to start with. I'm sure you can manage that." <<He>> pauses, then adds, "Broadly speaking, if you can't prepare what I've asked of you, <span class="purple">know that I'll always prefer that you serve something rather than nothing</span>."
<br><br>

<<if !$foodstuff.hamburger.knows_recipe and !$foodstuff.bread.knows_recipe>>
	<<link [[Say you don't know how to make hamburgers or bread|Mansion Intro 9 Recipe]]>><</link>>
<<elseif !$foodstuff.hamburger.knows_recipe>>
	<<link [[Say you don't know how to make hamburgers|Mansion Intro 9 Recipe]]>><</link>>
<<elseif !$foodstuff.bread.knows_recipe>>
	<<link [[Say you don't know how to make bread|Mansion Intro 9 Recipe]]>><</link>>
<<else>>
	Avery then turns to you with a smile and gestures to the mansion. "So, what do you think?"
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Say it's impressive|Mansion Intro 9 Impressive]]>><<npcincr Avery love 1>><</link>><<glove>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Say it's disappointing|Mansion Intro 9 Disappointing]]>><<npcincr Avery love -1>><</link>><<llove>>
	<br>

	/*
	<<link [[Push Avery into the pool|Mansion Intro 9 Push]]>><<npcincr Avery love -3>><<npcincr Avery dom -1>><<npcincr Avery rage 1>><</link>><<garage>><<lllove>><<ldom>>
	<br>
	*/
<</if>>

:: Mansion Intro 9 Recipe
<<effects>>
<<set $avery_mansion.study_unlocked to 1>><<set $daily.averyIntroRecipe to true>>
<<if !$foodstuff.hamburger.knows_recipe and !$foodstuff.bread.knows_recipe>>
	<<set _food to "hamburgers. Or bread, for the burgers">>
	<<set $avery_mansion.recipe.pushUnique("hamburger")>><<set $avery_mansion.recipe.pushUnique("bread")>>
<<elseif !$foodstuff.hamburger.knows_recipe>>
	<<set _food to "hamburgers">>
	<<set $avery_mansion.recipe.pushUnique("hamburger")>>
<<else>>
	<<set _food to "bread">>
	<<set $avery_mansion.recipe.pushUnique("bread")>>
<</if>>

<<speechresolve>>
<<if $speech_attitude_avery>>
	<<set _speechAttitudeResolved to "meek">>
<</if>>
<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy")>>
	"I... I don't actually know how to make _food," you admit, looking away.
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
	"I'm sorry," you say. "I don't know how to make _food yet."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
	"I can learn," you say quickly. "But I don't know how to make _food."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
	"I'll need a recipe first," you say. "I don't know how to make _food."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty">>
	"Hamburger's going to be a problem," you say. "I don't know how to make _food."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel">>
	"Then I hope you like disappointment," you say. "I don't know how to make _food."
<<else>>
	"I'm afraid I'm not sure how to make _food," you say.
<</if>>
<br><br>

Avery frowns. "Oh dear. What <i>are</i> they teaching you?" <<He>> produces a key, the same key <<he>> showed you previously, and gives it to you. "This goes to my study. Third storey, remember? I'm sure you'll find what you're looking for."
<br><br>

Once you've taken the key, <<he>> gestures to the mansion with a smile. "So, what do you think?"
<br><br>

<<link [[Say it's impressive|Mansion Intro 9 Impressive]]>><<npcincr Avery love 1>><</link>><<glove>>
<br>
<<link [[Say it's disappointing|Mansion Intro 9 Disappointing]]>><<npcincr Avery love -1>><</link>><<llove>>
<br>

/*
<<link [[Push Avery into the pool|Mansion Intro 9 Push]]>><<npcincr Avery love -3>><<npcincr Avery dom -1>><<npcincr Avery rage 1>><</link>><<garage>><<lllove>><<ldom>>
<br>
*/

:: Mansion Intro 9 Impressive
<<effects>>

<<speechresolve>>
<<if $speech_attitude_avery>>
	<<set _speechAttitudeResolved to "meek">>
<</if>>
<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy")>>
	"It's the most wonderful place I've ever seen," you say.
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
	"It's a beautiful home," you say. "You must be proud of it."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
	"It's lovely," you say. "I'll try to take proper care of it."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
	"It's impressive," you say. "I can see why you wanted to show it off."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty">>
	"It's pretty nice," you say.
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel">>
	"It's impressive," you say. "Very good at telling people what to think of you."
<<else>>
	"It's very impressive," you say.
<</if>>
<br><br>

Avery nods. "I'm glad you think so. It's your new home, after all. If you'll excuse me, I have some business to take care of."
<br><br>

<<He>> produces a phone from <<his>> pocket, and walks away while dialling.
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Mansion Pool]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Mansion Intro 9 Disappointing
<<effects>>

<<speechresolve>>
<<if $speech_attitude_avery>>
	<<set _speechAttitudeResolved to "meek">>
<</if>>
<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy")>>
	"It might be too posh for me," you say.
	<br><br>
	"Nonsense," Avery replies. "Don't act like an urchin I dragged in off the street. We'll have guests, and you'll need to show proper form."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
	"I'm sorry," you say. "I don't know what I'm supposed to think yet."
	<br><br>
	"Then let me help," Avery replies. "It's your home now. Treat it, and me, with respect."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
	"It's impressive," you say. "But I expected something warmer."
	<br><br>
	Avery's smile thins. "Warmth is something people bring with them. Perhaps you'll manage."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty">>
	"I was expecting something bigger," you say.
	<br><br>
	Avery draws <<himself>> up. <<He>> opens <<his>> mouth to reply, then reconsiders before speaking. "This is one of the finest mansions in town. If this doesn't suit you, then nowhere will."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel">>
	"It's tasteful," you say, looking around. "In the way a locked display case is tasteful."
	<br><br>
	Avery draws <<himself>> up. <<He>> opens <<his>> mouth to reply, then reconsiders before speaking. "You'll learn tact. Or you'll learn when to keep quiet."
<<else>>
	"It's a bit disappointing," you say.
	<br><br>
	"You'd better show more tact," Avery replies. "We'll have guests, and a mouth like that will reflect badly on us both."
<</if>>
<br><br>

"If you've no questions, I've business to take care of." <<He>> walks away before you can respond.
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Mansion Pool]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>
